      "html": "<p>O. dancena is an absolutely peaceful schooling fish that preferably swims near the water surface. It becomes about 4 cm long.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_dancena_en/",
      "html": "<p>Our O. dancena originate from the area around Calcutta in India, where they live along with such popular fish species as the zebra fish (Danio rerio) and the dwarf gourami (Colisa lalia).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_dancena_en/",
      "html": "<p>The elder hobbyists will know this nice blue-eye from India under the name of O. melastigmus; but this is another species, which is hardly ever kept in aquaria.</p>"
    }
